WEBVTT

00:16.350 --> 00:18.120
Dammit!

02:06.070 --> 02:07.140
Invincible!

02:07.140 --> 02:08.560
Rikkaidai!

02:08.560 --> 02:10.020
Seigaku!

02:10.020 --> 02:11.440
Fight!

02:12.040 --> 02:13.900
The strength of this year's Rikkai is,

02:13.900 --> 02:16.070
to put it bluntly, on a completely different level.

02:16.820 --> 02:20.450
The only ones who can prevent their third consecutive championship...

02:21.190 --> 02:23.410
is them.

02:25.910 --> 02:27.550
<i>This is bad!</i>

02:27.550 --> 02:29.620
<i>I'm going to be found out!</i>

02:32.200 --> 02:34.720
Is it true that Echizen didn't come?

02:34.720 --> 02:36.310
Yeah, that's right!

02:36.310 --> 02:40.150
Momoshiro-senpai went to get him, but...

02:41.240 --> 02:44.460
Are we going to continue with the finals even without Echizen?

02:44.990 --> 02:50.730
<b>We shall now commence with the National Tournament Finals: 
Rikkaidai Fuzoku versus Seishun Gakuen.</b>

02:54.900 --> 03:00.910
<b>Match one will be Singles 3: Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada versus Seishun Gakuen's Tezuka.</b>

03:03.810 --> 03:06.620
It's already the battle between those two?

03:06.620 --> 03:10.670
It's the competition everyone has been waiting for over the past three years,

03:10.670 --> 03:14.040
but who would've thought it'd be realized through such a decisive game?

03:23.800 --> 03:25.390
I won't let you off that easily.

03:29.710 --> 03:32.870
Vice-Captain Sanada seems really into this.

03:32.870 --> 03:36.190
One set match. Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada to serve.

03:36.660 --> 03:38.300
Let's go, Tezuka!

03:38.300 --> 03:40.360
I'll guide you to the depths of defeat!

03:47.220 --> 03:49.240
Swift like the Wind!

03:49.240 --> 03:50.680
FuuRinKaZan!

03:50.680 --> 03:52.410
What a fast swing!

03:53.870 --> 03:54.990
What!?

03:54.990 --> 03:57.290
Even Tezuka's getting serious right off the bat.

03:57.680 --> 03:59.220
Tezuka Zone.

04:05.800 --> 04:08.760
Silent like the Forest!

04:09.160 --> 04:12.220
<i>Whenever I drive Genichirou into a corner,</i>

04:12.220 --> 04:13.920
<i>from the moment he uses Forest,</i>

04:13.920 --> 04:16.690
<i>no matter what technique I use, it's effortlessly evaded.</i>

04:18.150 --> 04:20.890
If the ball lands over there, even Tezuka...

04:25.730 --> 04:26.740
In that case...

04:26.740 --> 04:29.430
Invade like Fire!

04:34.950 --> 04:37.000
He's even attacking with Fire already.

04:40.310 --> 04:43.090
Immovable like a Mountain.

04:43.840 --> 04:46.380
Mountain is the iron wall of defense.

04:46.380 --> 04:49.200
It's equally impossible to bring down.

04:49.200 --> 04:50.010
However...

04:55.980 --> 04:59.450
The Tezuka Zone... is amazing!

04:59.450 --> 05:00.900
That Sanada-kun is...

05:01.520 --> 05:03.870
The emperor is growing tired of attacking!

05:03.870 --> 05:05.420
As expected of Captain Tezuka!

05:05.420 --> 05:06.990
Absolute superiority!

05:06.990 --> 05:09.080
No, that's not it.

05:09.080 --> 05:11.440
Take a look around Tezuka's feet.

05:11.950 --> 05:14.420
The circles marking the boundaries around the zone...

05:14.420 --> 05:15.870
are blurring and growing larger.

05:19.890 --> 05:23.220
He's trying to defeat the Tezuka Zone in a head-on match.

05:27.310 --> 05:28.580
Take this,

05:28.580 --> 05:29.760
Tezuka!

05:44.410 --> 05:46.070
He moved in an instant!?

05:46.650 --> 05:50.590
The same way that Tezuka sealed Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami,

05:50.590 --> 05:54.040
Sanada sealed away two secret final moves.

05:54.420 --> 05:57.500
All for the sake of this day, so he could defeat Tezuka.

06:04.030 --> 06:05.390
15-0.

06:06.030 --> 06:09.010
Strike like Lightning!

06:09.480 --> 06:12.970
"Lightning"? There are more aside from FuuRinKaZan?

06:13.350 --> 06:16.220
Like lightning, he can appear anywhere.

06:16.220 --> 06:20.530
With a ball like a thunderbolt, he'll thrust you down to the bottom of despair.

06:20.530 --> 06:22.940
Once he uses that, it's the end;

06:22.940 --> 06:25.610
his opponents lose all their fighting spirit.

06:30.020 --> 06:31.620
That was a good shot.

06:32.260 --> 06:32.990
What!?

06:32.990 --> 06:37.160
Sorry, but our captain isn't the type to be scared off by lightning!

06:37.160 --> 06:39.580
If anything, it'll fire him up even more.

06:40.020 --> 06:41.040
Yeah.

06:47.420 --> 06:49.590
Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami!

06:51.610 --> 06:52.550
<i>That is...</i>

06:54.760 --> 06:57.470
Unpredictable like the Shadow!

06:57.470 --> 06:59.880
What!? "Unpredictable"?

06:59.880 --> 07:00.890
"Shadow"?

07:01.300 --> 07:05.310
That is the other final move Sanada sealed off;

07:05.950 --> 07:06.860
"Shadow."

07:07.330 --> 07:08.900
Without the slightest thread of an opening,

07:08.900 --> 07:12.310
it gives off the scent of various movement patterns,

07:12.310 --> 07:14.830
thereby sealing off Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami.

07:15.450 --> 07:17.370
FuuRinKaInZanRai.

07:17.880 --> 07:20.750
This is FuuRinKaZan's true form!

07:24.180 --> 07:26.030
What's wrong, Tezuka?

07:26.030 --> 07:27.600
You're looking pale.

07:28.630 --> 07:29.780
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

07:29.780 --> 07:30.550
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

07:30.550 --> 07:31.390
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

07:31.390 --> 07:32.120
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

07:32.120 --> 07:32.720
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

07:32.940 --> 07:35.510
Invade like Fire!

07:40.140 --> 07:43.770
Hyakuren Jitoku... Even though we told you it's pointless.

07:44.420 --> 07:47.230
Strike like Lightning!

07:50.190 --> 07:54.110
It's impossible to perceive the path of a flash of lightning.

08:00.230 --> 08:01.790
That's weak and useless!

08:09.800 --> 08:12.350
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada.

08:12.350 --> 08:13.970
2-0.

08:14.550 --> 08:18.720
Even Captain Tezuka... can't touch the ball!?

08:19.270 --> 08:23.040
Hyakuren Jitoku no Kiwami has been defeated by Lightning;

08:23.040 --> 08:27.520
Saikikanpatsu no Kiwami has been sealed off by Shadow.

08:27.520 --> 08:29.690
How unsightly, Tezuka.

08:36.620 --> 08:38.990
It seems like it's a one-sided match in Sanada's favor.

08:38.990 --> 08:39.910
No way!

08:39.910 --> 08:42.920
There's no way Captain Tezuka would ever lose!

08:43.820 --> 08:46.000
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada.

08:46.000 --> 08:47.380
3-0.

08:48.240 --> 08:50.800
Sanada-kun is very strict on others,

08:50.800 --> 08:53.260
but he's even stricter with himself.

08:53.260 --> 08:55.600
The Kanto District Tournament loss...

08:55.600 --> 08:58.680
placed an unfathomable weight on Genichirou's shoulders.

08:58.680 --> 09:03.490
Honestly speaking, the only one who can defeat the current Sanada is me.

09:03.490 --> 09:05.320
Are you bragging?

09:05.960 --> 09:08.200
It's self-confidence.

09:08.200 --> 09:09.610
There it is!

09:09.610 --> 09:11.480
Captain Tezuka's electrifying weapon.

09:11.480 --> 09:13.550
The Zero Shiki Drop Shot!

09:15.820 --> 09:17.990
T-The Zero Shiki Drop is...

09:23.090 --> 09:24.450
Weak, weak...

09:24.450 --> 09:25.540
Weak!

09:27.440 --> 09:28.580
Nothing can be done!?

09:33.120 --> 09:34.210
Tezuka Zone!?

09:44.770 --> 09:46.400
Tezuka Zone was... defeated...

09:46.400 --> 09:48.270
Tezuka Zone was... defeated...

09:49.280 --> 09:50.690
head-on.

09:51.260 --> 09:53.610
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada.

09:53.610 --> 09:55.180
4-0.

09:57.400 --> 10:01.320
There's nothing left for you except the path of defeat, Tezuka.

10:07.120 --> 10:09.760
Now then, what will you do?

10:09.760 --> 10:13.020
It would seem as if there is no way to return your shots.

10:13.980 --> 10:16.630
Does that mean you've accepted your defeat?

10:16.630 --> 10:19.630
I did not say there was no way to defeat you.

10:22.380 --> 10:24.010
Nonsense.

10:32.730 --> 10:35.400
We will achieve our Rikkai's third consecutive championship!{added dai, wonder if makes much difference? -juggen}

10:41.440 --> 10:43.700
Strike like Lightning!

10:44.700 --> 10:46.160
It's the Tezuka Zone again!

10:46.160 --> 10:48.330
Don't you{Do you not} understand that it's futile!?

10:48.330 --> 10:50.080
It's impossible to return Lightning!

10:53.340 --> 10:55.080
You can't, Tezuka!

10:57.340 --> 10:59.760
Out! 0-15.

11:00.140 --> 11:01.180
What!?

11:02.760 --> 11:04.680
If it's a ball that can't be returned,

11:05.780 --> 11:07.640
then it's fine if I don't return it.

11:12.410 --> 11:14.460
<b><i>Why doesn't the Tezuka Zone...</i></b>

11:14.460 --> 11:16.470
<b><i>just make all of the opponent's shots go out?</i></b>

11:17.150 --> 11:18.360
<b><i>It's impossible.</i></b>

11:18.360 --> 11:19.980
<b><i>Why?</i></b>

11:19.980 --> 11:24.480
<b><i>In the case of singles, if you stand at the center mark,</i></b>

11:24.480 --> 11:27.330
<b><i>you will be at the center of 8.23 meters...</i></b>

11:27.330 --> 11:32.470
<b><i>from which you will have a 1.5 meter radius to cover with a turn.</i></b>

11:33.220 --> 11:36.210
<b><i>If your opponent aims for the corner's edge,</i></b>

11:36.210 --> 11:40.240
<b><i>the zone will be complete if in the 2.6 meters to the right or left you add a spin in advance,</i></b>

11:40.240 --> 11:44.230
<b><i>controlling the ball to be drawn in towards yourself.</i></b>

11:44.230 --> 11:47.970
<b><i>However, in the case of making the shots go out,</i></b>

11:47.970 --> 11:52.370
<b><i>if the ball is hit down the center, you'll have a 4.2 meter radius to shift.</i></b>

11:52.370 --> 11:55.270
<b><i>You also have to add an outward spin to the ball to force it out.</i></b>

11:55.670 --> 11:58.490
<b><i>That may have been a bit difficult for you.</i></b>

11:59.330 --> 12:01.240
<b><i>So basically,</i></b>

12:01.630 --> 12:03.620
<b><i>it's possible, right?</i></b>

12:09.580 --> 12:11.600
Making all of my shots go out?

12:11.600 --> 12:13.040
Such a thing...

12:13.040 --> 12:14.420
is impossible!

12:23.150 --> 12:24.030
Out!

12:24.030 --> 12:25.650
Game, Seigaku's Tezuka.

12:25.650 --> 12:27.430
1-4.

12:33.340 --> 12:35.730
Let's not get careless.

12:36.890 --> 12:37.690
Momoshiro.

12:38.060 --> 12:40.690
It seems that Tezuka has begun his counter-attack.

12:40.690 --> 12:41.820
As expected of the captain!

12:41.820 --> 12:43.700
That's how it should be!

12:43.700 --> 12:46.320
However, he's going to sacrifice his arm a second time to do it.

12:52.910 --> 12:53.750
Out!

12:53.750 --> 12:55.410
Game, Seigaku's Tezuka.

12:55.410 --> 12:57.000
2-4.

12:57.000 --> 12:57.980
Amazing!

12:57.980 --> 13:00.490
That reverse Tezuka Zone is just too awesome!

13:00.490 --> 13:04.160
No, it would lay waste to even the Tezuka Zone.

13:04.160 --> 13:06.640
It's an illusion that is impossible to grasp.

13:07.470 --> 13:10.140
In other words, Tezuka Phantom.

13:12.340 --> 13:13.850
You can't...

13:13.850 --> 13:16.100
You can't, Tezuka!

13:17.120 --> 13:18.500
Tezuka,

13:18.500 --> 13:22.980
are you going to do it again for the sake of our team?

13:24.210 --> 13:26.400
What's going on, Ryuzaki-sensei?

13:28.320 --> 13:29.780
Sensei!?

13:30.120 --> 13:33.700
A rotation six times greater than the Tezuka Zone?

13:33.700 --> 13:35.830
He said before...

13:35.830 --> 13:37.370
that it was impossible.

13:37.370 --> 13:39.210
O-Obviously!

13:41.040 --> 13:42.670
If he were to do that,

13:43.300 --> 13:45.180
the burden on his arm would be...

13:46.700 --> 13:48.050
No way.{such a thing...}

13:52.210 --> 13:53.430
Tezuka...

13:54.900 --> 13:56.650
Game, Seigaku's Tezuka.

13:56.650 --> 13:58.350
3-4.

14:00.440 --> 14:02.320
You should leave it at that.

14:02.320 --> 14:04.980
You'll become unable to play tennis ever again.

14:10.950 --> 14:12.410
<i>Fool.</i>

14:15.580 --> 14:17.250
<i>How long do you think you can keep this up?</i>

14:21.690 --> 14:23.250
15-0.

14:24.210 --> 14:25.880
Zero Shiki Serve?

14:26.390 --> 14:31.300
<i>Hyakuren Jitoku, Tezuka Zone, and Tezuka Phantom.</i>

14:31.300 --> 14:33.850
<i>And on top of that, even the Zero Shiki Serve?</i>

14:35.270 --> 14:36.270
30-0.

14:37.160 --> 14:39.730
Please... stop already.

14:41.810 --> 14:43.110
40-0.

14:46.640 --> 14:48.500
Why are you... always like that?

14:48.500 --> 14:50.200
Why are you... always like that?

14:51.930 --> 14:56.610
<b><i>I want to win the national tournament with everyone.</i></b>

14:56.610 --> 14:59.160
<b><i>For the sake of becoming a pro, I'm thinking of going to Germany.</i></b>

15:00.310 --> 15:01.080
<b><i>That's why,</i></b>

15:02.530 --> 15:06.050
<b><i>no matter what, I don't want to leave behind any regrets.{regret}</i></b>

15:07.740 --> 15:08.890
Tezuka...

15:11.860 --> 15:13.590
Game, Seigaku's Tezuka.

15:13.590 --> 15:15.180
4-4.

15:16.430 --> 15:18.280
Captain Tezuka's arm is...

15:18.970 --> 15:22.020
It's congested with blood and swollen!

15:22.170 --> 15:24.420
In addition to the barrage of Tezuka Phantoms,

15:24.420 --> 15:26.570
he used the Zero Shiki Serve four times in a row.

15:26.570 --> 15:32.470
It wouldn't be unusual for 99.9% of players to be beyond hope of recovery.

15:36.580 --> 15:38.390
Vice-Captain Sanada!

15:38.390 --> 15:40.580
You've overused Lightning, huh.

15:41.750 --> 15:45.520
Lightning, in which you use your legs violently to move, is a godlike skill.

15:45.520 --> 15:47.530
After using it so many times consecutively,

15:47.530 --> 15:49.790
there's no way his legs wouldn't reach their limit.

15:52.650 --> 15:53.690
Fine.

15:53.690 --> 15:56.220
I'll take on your resolution!

16:01.180 --> 16:02.890
H-He's still using Lightning!?

16:04.150 --> 16:05.860
0-15.

16:05.860 --> 16:08.780
Tezuka can still use Phantom?

16:09.150 --> 16:10.690
Those two...

16:10.690 --> 16:12.650
How far will they go for their head-on battle!?

16:13.540 --> 16:14.400
Out!

16:14.400 --> 16:16.000
Game, Seigaku's Tezuka.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.080
5-4.

16:18.560 --> 16:20.520
Arai, prepare some ice!

16:20.520 --> 16:21.550
Hurry!

16:27.110 --> 16:28.710
Tezuka...

16:29.500 --> 16:31.180
Let's not get careless.

16:31.180 --> 16:32.130
I know.

16:32.970 --> 16:34.200
Because... we came to win.

16:34.200 --> 16:36.510
Because... we came to win.

16:38.360 --> 16:40.960
Are you telling me to abandon the head-on battle?

16:40.960 --> 16:43.660
Tezuka can no longer use his Zero Shiki Serve.

16:43.660 --> 16:45.900
The next game will decide the match.

16:45.900 --> 16:48.820
Everything is for the sake of Rikkai's third consecutive championship.

16:56.160 --> 17:00.080
So he really has gotten to the point of being unable to use the Zero Shiki Serve...

17:01.270 --> 17:02.010
There it is!

17:02.010 --> 17:03.540
Tezuka Phantom!

17:03.910 --> 17:06.210
Strike like Lightning!

17:07.300 --> 17:08.120
Combined with...

17:08.120 --> 17:11.750
Silent like the Forest! {ambient: I suggest split.}

17:11.750 --> 17:15.590
Vice-Captain Sanada... abandoned the head-on challenge!?

17:18.970 --> 17:22.770
With that, the spin on Tezuka's shots will only lessen,

17:22.770 --> 17:25.570
so it won't be able to end Sanada's point.

17:25.570 --> 17:27.300
That's what they're aiming for.

17:28.200 --> 17:31.130
In a situation where he doesn't know when Lightning will come,

17:31.130 --> 17:33.940
he'll have no choice but to continually use Tezuka Phantom.

17:34.440 --> 17:35.320
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

17:35.320 --> 17:36.110
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

17:36.110 --> 17:36.900
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

17:36.900 --> 17:37.660
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

17:37.660 --> 17:38.320
Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor! Emperor!

17:38.940 --> 17:40.840
<i>How is this being an emperor?</i>

17:40.840 --> 17:43.080
<i>What part of me, who's abandoned this head-on challenge,</i>

17:43.080 --> 17:45.330
<i>are you calling an emperor!?</i>

17:45.330 --> 17:47.660
Game, Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada.

17:47.660 --> 17:49.250
6-5.

17:51.930 --> 17:53.380
<i>It's fine like that.</i>

18:02.680 --> 18:03.850
40-0.

18:03.850 --> 18:06.560
The match point's already been decided.

18:08.270 --> 18:11.190
Even after coming this far, he can still use Tezuka Phantom?

18:11.660 --> 18:15.650
Tezuka, you won't let your guard down even to the last second.

18:16.160 --> 18:18.240
You're prepared for Lightning.

18:23.510 --> 18:28.010
Tezuka, for the end, I'll take on your head-on challenge!

18:28.980 --> 18:31.920
Strike like Lightning!

18:34.040 --> 18:34.840
The shot isn't...

18:34.840 --> 18:36.800
going out!

18:36.800 --> 18:38.890
Tezuka Phantom...

18:38.890 --> 18:39.930
was defeated!

18:41.130 --> 18:41.890
No, wait!

18:42.370 --> 18:44.430
The shot is being drawn in towards Tezuka!

18:44.810 --> 18:45.990
That... isn't Tezuka Phantom.

18:45.990 --> 18:47.890
That... isn't Tezuka Phantom.

18:47.890 --> 18:49.440
Tezuka Zone!

18:54.900 --> 18:56.590
It's over.

18:56.590 --> 18:58.150
No, not yet.

18:59.450 --> 19:01.280
Tezuka isn't done just yet.

19:02.250 --> 19:05.200
<i>He added a spin to the ball!</i>

19:05.200 --> 19:07.080
<i>Even though your racket was blown away,</i>

19:07.080 --> 19:09.160
<i>you returned Lightning!?</i>

19:09.990 --> 19:12.500
The winners will be us, Seigaku!

19:13.170 --> 19:13.960
And then...

19:16.050 --> 19:18.800
Seigaku's era will be established once again!

19:22.500 --> 19:23.530
<i>Move!</i>

19:23.530 --> 19:26.100
<i>Can't these legs move!?</i>

19:28.140 --> 19:30.250
There's no way...

19:30.250 --> 19:34.020
There's no way I will lose!

19:36.140 --> 19:40.440
<i>From the time he appeared around three years ago,</i>

19:42.150 --> 19:45.010
<i>even while winning two consecutive championships,</i>

19:45.010 --> 19:48.350
<i>I've always felt this ill feeling...</i>

19:48.350 --> 19:51.190
<i>because I haven't been able to defeat him!</i>

19:59.930 --> 20:01.180
<i>Shit!</i>

20:01.180 --> 20:02.470
<i>Just a little bit...</i>

20:02.470 --> 20:04.050
<i>to the other side...</i>

20:04.760 --> 20:08.210
Fall on the other side!

20:12.540 --> 20:15.350
<b>Game and match, Rikkaidai Fuzoku's Sanada.</b>

20:15.350 --> 20:17.150
<b>7-5.</b>

20:23.280 --> 20:24.390
Tezuka,

20:25.610 --> 20:29.080
I'm never doing this with you again.

22:11.850 --> 22:13.490
Amnesia!?

22:13.490 --> 22:17.480
I'm sorry. I was brought here all of a sudden and don't really understand what's going on.

22:17.480 --> 22:18.140
Sadaharu,

22:18.140 --> 22:20.970
the Tornado Snake isn't effective against this guy when his eyes are red.

22:20.970 --> 22:23.020
I have collected all of your data.

22:23.400 --> 22:26.490
Of course, that includes red-eyed Kirihara's data.

22:26.490 --> 22:29.160
If the data you've collected were fake, what would you do? {you added}

22:29.160 --> 22:31.280
Next time: Our Way of Doing Things.

22:34.580 --> 22:36.570
Should I dye you red as well?

22:36.570 --> 22:38.360
W-What's with that person?

22:38.360 --> 22:40.330
Isn't he way too scary?
